0. WHAT IS IT?

This is a PHP frontend end to vnstat, a network traffic logger.
Since vnstat is console mode only I created this script to
make a 'nice' report of the data collected by vnstat.
For more information about vnstat check out http://humdi.net/vnstat/
For updates to this script check http://www.sqweek.com


1. REQUIREMENTS 

- vnstat setup and collecting data
- webserver with PHP
- php-gd extension installed for PNG graphs
- php-intl extension for month and weekday names in the language of the
  locale set in config.php (optional, without it they stay in english)


2. INSTALL

Installation should be really straightforward:

Put the files from this package somewhere inside the webroot of
your webserver. Then edit the few configuration options in config.php
to suit your situation and your good to go. The various options are
explained in config.php.


3. THEMES

Two themes are included, 'light' and 'dark'. Both share the layout in
themes/base.css and only define their own palette in themes/<name>/style.css;
themes/<name>/theme.php holds the matching colours for the graph images
drawn by graph.php and graph_svg.php.

On top of those there is 'auto', which loads the light palette and lets the
dark one take over when the browser reports the device is in dark mode. It
needs no javascript, so the page never shows up in the wrong palette first.
The graph images can't follow the device though, they are drawn on the
server: with 'auto' they are drawn in the light colours, which only matters
when $graph_format is set to svg or png.

The theme can be switched from the sidebar, or by adding style=auto,
style=light or style=dark to the url. The theme used when nothing is
selected is set with DEFAULT_COLORSCHEME in config.php.

The webfonts the themes use are served from the fonts/ directory, so the
frontend does not talk to any third party.


